# NOTE: .git/ is intentionally NOT ignored. The hosted gate needs git
# metadata: tests/test_release_manifest.py requires `git rev-parse HEAD`
# (fail-closed "untraceable source state" otherwise), and manifest/ISO
# generation records the source commit. A git-less tarball reds the whole
# python-tests step (13 failures) and would break manifest provenance.
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
dist/
*.iso
*.img
*.raw
web-preview/
.ai/memory/*.local.md
.DS_Store
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ci-cache/
packaging/live/cache/
packaging/live/chroot/
packaging/live/.build/
packaging/live/.stage/
packaging/live/binary/
packaging/live/tmp/
# live-build creates local config files and absolute hook symlinks during lb
# config. Uploading those stale outputs can break source packaging on macOS.
packaging/live/config/binary
packaging/live/config/bootstrap
packaging/live/config/chroot
packaging/live/config/common
packaging/live/config/source
packaging/live/config/package-lists/live.list.chroot
packaging/live/config/hooks/live/
packaging/live/config/hooks/normal/*.hook.chroot
!packaging/live/config/hooks/normal/0500-build-nwipe.hook.chroot
# Generated live-build copies of src/. Uploading a stale local tree makes
# test_staged_chroot_package_matches_src fail before the ISO step restages.
packaging/live/config/includes.chroot/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/beamo_wipe/
packaging/live/config/includes.chroot/usr/share/beamo-wipe/
packaging/live/config/includes.chroot/usr/share/doc/beamo-wipe/
.env.*
# Keep local captures, caches, and generated live-build files out of uploads.
# This project deliberately retains .git/ so hosted build provenance works.
#!include:.gitignore
